              "Mr. Trump said the deal would result in an additional $40 billion to $50 billion in farm purchases by China.\n\nSo far the agreement is in principle only. The deal will take three to five weeks to put on paper, officials said. And despite the ceasefire, a broader trade deal faces significant obstacles, according to analysts with Eurasia Group, a political risk consultancy",
